# gnome-touchpad-gestures
#
# Lets the user at the active seat read the touchpad and create virtual
# input devices. Must sort before 73-seat-late.rules.
#
# Note what the second line allows: any program run by that user can create
# input devices and so type and click as the user. On X11 any program can
# already do that through XTest.
# A device that is a keyboard as well as a touchpad is left alone, so that
# nothing here makes keystrokes readable.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHPAD}=="1", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}!="1", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", TAG+="uaccess", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
